//! Gauss-Legendre 120-point atmospheric-ray quadrature.
//!
//! Generated dimensionless nodes and weights from `libephemeris/refraction.py`
//! at`37ffb0555b7a9f5083b4f1b6dc1a0f10feeb85fa` (v3.2.1),
//! blob`88d0f6230d8a88e2dc98bf2cfbf20b273ff5ab99`.
//! The construction uses the Legendre recurrence, Newton-Raphson refinement
//! with Tricomi starting values and a 1 e-15 step criterion. Values are stored as
//! binary64 bit patterns; do not edit generated data.
//!
//! Nodes lie inside[-1,1] in symmetric pairs, with extremes
//! ±0.999800865658959. Weights follow the same order and sum to 2 within
//! one ULP. The Green-integral ray tracer uses the fixed 120-point rule after
//! desingularizing its radial coordinate. Physical lengths, atmospheric model,
//! angle domain and index errors belong to the consuming refraction kernel.

